Attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

engine/ contains an INDEPENDENT, CLEAN-ROOM reimplementation of the SPARQL
provenance query-rewriting introduced by NPCS:

  Zubaria Asma, Daniel Hernández, Luis Galárraga, Giorgos Flouris,
  Irini Fundulaki, and Katja Hose.
  "NPCS: Native Provenance Computation for SPARQL."
  Proceedings of the ACM Web Conference 2024 (WWW), pp. 2085–2093.
  https://doi.org/10.1145/3589334.3645557

This reimplementation was written from the published algorithm (rewriting rules
in the paper). It does NOT include, copy, or derive from the original NPCS source
code or the `ReifySparqlByte.jar` binary. The BGP rewriting was verified to match
the original's output by black-box differential testing on the WatDiv query set;
non-monotone operators (OPTIONAL/MINUS) follow the paper's semantics.

